nums, return an array answer such that answer[i] is equal to the product of=
 all the elements of nums except nums[i].

The product of any prefix or suffix of nums is guaranteed to fit in a 32-bi=
t integer.

You must write an algorithm that runs in&nbsp;O(n)&nbsp;time and without us=
ing the division operation.

&nbsp;

Example 1:

Input: nums =3D [1,2,3,4]
Output: [24,12,8,6]


Example 2:

Input: nums =3D [-1,1,0,-3,3]
Output: [0,0,9,0,0]


&nbsp;

Constraints:

 * 2 &lt;=3D nums.length &lt;=3D 105
 * -30 &lt;=3D nums[i] &lt;=3D 30
 * The input is generated such that answer[i] is guaranteed to fit in a 32-=
bit integer.

&nbsp;

